var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"messages/#Messages","page":"Messages","text":"Besides traits, some widgets exchange custom messages with the host: a heartbeat, samples of a chart, a sync_request from a new view. Each widget class lists its messages in the contract:\n\nusing AnywidgetInstruments\n[(m[\"type\"], m[\"direction\"]) for m in message_specs(\"TrendChart\")]\n5-element Vector{Tuple{String, String}}:\n (\"hb\", \"host-to-front\")\n (\"append\", \"host-to-front\")\n (\"snapshot\", \"host-to-front\")\n (\"clear\", \"host-to-front\")\n (\"sync_request\", \"front-to-host\")","title":"Messages"},{"category":"section","location":"messages/#Building-messages","page":"Messages","text":"A Message is a JSON content and a list of binary buffers. Builders check the message type against the contract:\n\ntrend = TrendChart(; pens = [Dict(\"name\" => \"Level\"), Dict(\"name\" => \"Temperature\")])\nm = append_message(trend, [[1.7e9, 1.7e9 + 1], [1.7e9]], [[0.5, 0.6], [20.0]])\nm.content\nDict{String, Any} with 2 entries:\n  \"type\" => \"append\"\n  \"pens\" => Any[Any[0, 2, 2], Any[1, 1, 1]]\n\nlength.(m.buffers)   # float64 times and float32 values for each pen\n4-element Vector{Int64}:\n 16\n  8\n  8\n  4\n\nBuilder Widgets\nheartbeat_message every widget (HOST-003)\nappend_message(w, values) Sparkline, KPITile\nappend_message(w, times, values), snapshot_message TrendChart\nmessage(w, type; fields...) any message without buffers (clear, latch_expired, …)\n\nencode_buffer writes the buffers of other messages: numpy-style dtype, little-endian whatever the host.","title":"Building messages"},{"category":"section","location":"messages/#Sending-messages","page":"Messages","text":"send_message hands a message to the transport of the host, with the widget's message id (w.id). The Kaimon Slate extension installs one when SlateAFM is loaded; another host installs its own:\n\nAnywidgetInstruments.set_transport!((id, msg) -> my_send(id, msg.content, msg.buffers))","title":"Sending messages"},{"category":"section","location":"messages/#Heartbeats","page":"Messages","text":"A host announcing heartbeats sets _session and _heartbeat on the widgets, then sends heartbeat_message every _heartbeat seconds to at least one widget of the session. Without heartbeats, the widgets never show ⚠ NO KERNEL or ⚠ STALE.","title":"Heartbeats"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-reference","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"API reference"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Contract,-widgets,-encoding,-messages-and-rules","page":"API reference","text":"","title":"Contract, widgets, encoding, messages and rules"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Widget-constructors","page":"API reference","text":"One constructor per concrete class of anywidget-instruments, generated from the trait contract. Pipe is not exported (Base exports a Pipe type): call it AnywidgetInstruments.Pipe.","title":"Widget constructors"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.AnywidgetInstruments","page":"API reference","text":"AnywidgetInstruments\n\nInstrumentation widgets (knobs, gauges, tanks, LEDs, strip charts, alarms, supervisory objects) for Julia, from the front end of the Python package anywidget-instruments.\n\nThe package ships the front-end module and its trait contract: a widget is a class name and a dictionary of traits checked against that contract. Hosts render it:\n\nany environment showing HTML, through the standalone text/html display;\nKaimonSlate.jl, through the SlateAFM extension (package extension on SlateExtensionsBase).\n\nusing AnywidgetInstruments\nlevel = Tank(1.2; max = 5, unit = \"m\", hi = 4.5, show_limits = true, label = \"Level\")\nlevel[:value] = 2.0\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.AnywidgetInstruments"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Instrument","page":"API reference","text":"Instrument\n\nA widget of anywidget-instruments: its class (\"Tank\", \"Knob\", …), a message id and the traits set by the user, stored in their JSON form and checked against the trait contract.\n\nBuild one with the class constructors (Tank(3.2; max = 4)) or instrument. Read and update traits like a dictionary: w[:value], w[:value] = 2.0. traits gives the dictionary a host binds the front end to.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Instrument"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Message","page":"API reference","text":"Message(content, buffers = Vector{UInt8}[])\n\nA custom message: its JSON content (with a \"type\" field) and its binary buffers, sent with it in order (little-endian bytes, see encode_buffer).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.alarm_level-Tuple{Real}","page":"API reference","text":"alarm_level(value; lolo = nothing, lo = nothing, hi = nothing, hihi = nothing,\n            deadband = 0, previous = \"normal\") -> String\n\nAlarm level of value (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\" or \"hihi\", ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Limits are inclusive; nothing is an unset limit. Entering a more severe level is immediate; leaving a level requires the value to move back beyond that level's limit by at least deadband. A non-finite value keeps the previous level.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.alarm_level"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.append_message-Tuple{Instrument, AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API reference","text":"append_message(w, times, values; totals = nothing) -> Message\n\nNew samples of the pens of a TrendChart: times[i] (Unix seconds) and values[i] are the samples of pen i (in the order of the pens trait); pens without samples are skipped. totals[i] is the number of samples of pen i since the last clear (default: the samples sent). One float64 time buffer and one float32 value buffer are sent per pen.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.append_message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.append_message-Tuple{Instrument, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"append_message(w, values) -> Message\n\nNew values of a Sparkline or a KPITile (a number or a vector, oldest first): {\"type\": \"append\", \"n\"} and one float32 buffer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.append_message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.asset_source-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"asset_source() -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nOrigin of the vendored front end (assets/SOURCE.toml): package, version, wheel file name and its SHA-256 checksum (JL-GEN-004).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.asset_source"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.assets_dir-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"assets_dir() -> String\n\nDirectory of the vendored front end: index.js, index.css, contract.json, schema/*.schema.json, templates/*.svg, the license of anywidget-instruments and SOURCE.toml.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.assets_dir"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.class_of_kind-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"class_of_kind(kind) -> String\n\nClass of a widget kind (\"tank\" → \"Tank\").\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.class_of_kind"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.coerce_value-Tuple{Real, Real, Real, Bool}","page":"API reference","text":"coerce_value(value, min, max, coerce) -> value\n\nValue as the kernel stores it: clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set and the value is finite (NUM-006, NUM-010).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.coerce_value"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.decode_nonfinite-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"decode_nonfinite(x)\n\nInverse of encode_nonfinite: \"nan\", \"inf\", \"-inf\" (and \"NaN\", \"Infinity\", \"-Infinity\") become Float64; other values are returned unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.decode_nonfinite"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.default_traits-Tuple{Union{AbstractString, Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"default_traits(class) -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nEvery trait of a class with its default value; non-finite defaults are decoded to Float64 (JL-CON-005).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.default_traits"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.encode_buffer-Tuple{AbstractString, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"encode_buffer(dtype, values) -> Vector{UInt8}\n\nBytes of a binary buffer of a contract dtype (\"<f4\", \"<f8\", \"u1\", \"uint8\", \"<i4\", …): each value is converted to the element type and written little-endian, whatever the byte order of the host (JL-ENC-004).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.encode_buffer"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.encode_nonfinite-Tuple{Real}","page":"API reference","text":"encode_nonfinite(x)\n\nWire form of a number: NaN, Inf and -Inf become \"nan\", \"inf\" and \"-inf\" (JSON has no such numbers); any other value is returned unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.encode_nonfinite"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.frontend_version-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"frontend_version() -> String\n\nVersion of anywidget-instruments whose front end is vendored (JL-CON-001).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.frontend_version"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.heartbeat_message-Tuple{AbstractString, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"heartbeat_message(session, interval) -> Message\n\nThe heartbeat {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\", \"interval\"} a host sends every _heartbeat seconds to announce that it is alive (HOST-003).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.heartbeat_message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.html_page-Tuple{Vararg{Instrument}}","page":"API reference","text":"html_page(widgets...; title = \"AnywidgetInstruments\") -> String\nhtml_page(path, widgets...; title = \"AnywidgetInstruments\") -> path\n\nA standalone HTML page showing widgets side by side, the front-end module included once (JL-HTML-005). With a path, the page is written to that file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.html_page"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.instrument-Tuple{Union{AbstractString, Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"instrument(class; id = <unique>, traits...) -> Instrument\ninstrument(class, value; id = <unique>, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA widget of class class (a String or a Symbol) with the given traits. Every trait is checked against the contract: an unknown trait or a value that does not conform throws an ArgumentError; a number outside the inclusive bounds of its spec is clamped. id names the widget's message channel for hosts routing custom messages.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.instrument"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.merge_traits-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"merge_traits(d::AbstractDict; traits...) -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nA copy of the trait dictionary d (for example the bound value of a widget in a notebook host) with some traits changed and checked like the constructors do; the class is found from d[\"_kind\"]. Derived traits are updated when the host owns the state (JL-API-014).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.merge_traits"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.message-Tuple{Instrument, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"message(w, type; strict = true, fields...) -> Message\n\nA message of type for widget w with JSON fields and no buffer. With strict = true, type must be a host-to-front message of the class in the contract (JL-MSG-005).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.message_specs-Tuple{Union{AbstractString, Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"message_specs(class) -> Vector{Any}\n\nCustom messages of a widget class: type, direction, fields, buffers (JL-CON-003).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.message_specs"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.normalize_value_labels-Tuple{Any}","page":"API reference","text":"normalize_value_labels(items) -> Vector{@NamedTuple{value::Float64, label::String}}\n\nUsable value labels sorted by value (IND-118): an item lacking a finite numeric value or a non-blank label is dropped; of two items with the same value the first is kept. Items are dictionaries (string or symbol keys) or named tuples.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.normalize_value_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.send_message-Tuple{Instrument, Message}","page":"API reference","text":"send_message(w, msg::Message)\nsend_message(id, msg::Message)\n\nSend a message to the views of widget w (or of message id id) through the installed transport (see set_transport!).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.send_message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.set_asset_base!-Tuple{Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"API reference","text":"set_asset_base!(url::Union{AbstractString,Nothing})\n\nBase URL the HTML display loads index.js and index.css from (for example the directory where a documentation build copied assets_dir). nothing (the default) inlines them in each output, which makes the output self-contained but about 1 MB larger (JL-HTML-003, JL-HTML-004).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.set_asset_base!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.set_transport!-Tuple{Any}","page":"API reference","text":"set_transport!(f)\n\nInstall the function sending messages to the front end: f(id, msg::Message), id being the widget's message id. Host integrations install one (the KaimonSlate.jl extension sends through SlateAFM); nothing removes it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.set_transport!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.snapshot_message-Tuple{Instrument, AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API reference","text":"snapshot_message(w, times, values; totals = nothing) -> Message\n\nKept samples of every pen of a TrendChart, in reply to sync_request; the arguments are those of append_message.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.snapshot_message"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.to_json-Tuple{Any}","page":"API reference","text":"to_json(w; defaults = false) -> String\n\nJSON text of the traits of a widget, as a host hands them to the front end (JL-ENC-003). With defaults = true, every trait of the class is included.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.to_json"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.trait_specs-Tuple{Union{AbstractString, Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"trait_specs(class) -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nTrait specs of a widget class, keyed by trait name, as in contract.json (type, default, writer, bounds, …). The returned dictionary is shared: do not mutate it (JL-CON-003).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.trait_specs"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.traits-Tuple{Instrument}","page":"API reference","text":"traits(w::Instrument; defaults = false) -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nThe trait dictionary of a widget in its JSON form (non-finite numbers as \"nan\", \"inf\", \"-inf\"): the traits set by the user and _kind, or, with defaults = true, every trait of the class (JL-API-010).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.traits"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.update-Tuple{Instrument}","page":"API reference","text":"update(w::Instrument; traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA copy of w, with the same id, where some traits are changed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.update"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.valid_scale","page":"API reference","text":"valid_scale(min, max, scale = \"linear\") -> Bool\n\nA usable scale: finite bounds, max > min, and min > 0 on a \"log\" scale.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.valid_scale"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.value_label_of-Tuple{Any, Real, Real, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"value_label_of(labels, value, lo, hi) -> Union{String,Nothing}\n\nLabel of value within 1e-9 of the scale span [lo, hi], or nothing. labels comes from normalize_value_labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.value_label_of"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.value_of_label-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"value_of_label(labels, text) -> Union{Float64,Nothing}\n\nValue of the label text, ignoring case and surrounding spaces, or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.value_of_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.widget_class-Tuple{Instrument}","page":"API reference","text":"widget_class(w::Instrument) -> String\n\nClass name of a widget (\"Tank\", …).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.widget_class"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.widget_classes-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"widget_classes() -> Vector{String}\n\nNames of the concrete widget classes of the contract, sorted (JL-CON-002).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.widget_classes"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.widget_kind-Tuple{Union{AbstractString, Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"widget_kind(class) -> String\n\nValue of the _kind trait of a class: it selects the view of the front end.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.widget_kind"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.wrap_modulo-Tuple{Real, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"wrap_modulo(value, modulo)\n\nA finite value wrapped into [0, modulo) (a compass heading); a non-finite value is returned unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.wrap_modulo"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.AlarmBanner","page":"API reference","text":"AlarmBanner(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA AlarmBanner widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"alarmbanner\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [520,180]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; derived): Alarms that are not back to normal, {id, timestamp, source, priority, message, state}; the view sorts them (unacknowledged first, then priority and time). Written by the host (Python: raise_alarm(), clear_alarm()); without a host owning the state, the front end applies the acknowledgements (an alarm back to normal leaves the list) and writes the list back (HOST-004, HOST-012).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.AlarmBanner"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.AlarmIndicator","page":"API reference","text":"AlarmIndicator(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nAlarmIndicator(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA AlarmIndicator widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"alarmindicator\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_id (string; default \"\"; host): Identifier passed to the acknowledgement callbacks.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmessage (string; default \"\"; host): Alarm message (plain text, SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npriority (\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"critical\"; default \"high\"; host): Priority, shown by a shape and a P1 .. P4 text as well as a color (A11Y-003).\nsize (array; default [260,64]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (\"normal\", \"active_unacknowledged\", \"active_acknowledged\", \"cleared_unacknowledged\"; default \"normal\"; host and operator): ISA-18.2 alarm state. Transitions (x-awi-transitions, [state, event, next]): activate and clear come from the host; acknowledge from the operator (ACK), applied by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end, which always sends the ack message (HOST-012).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.AlarmIndicator"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.AlarmList","page":"API reference","text":"AlarmList(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA AlarmList widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"alarmlist\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmax_shelve (number; default 28800; host): Longest shelving allowed, in seconds (IND-051).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nshelve_durations (array; default [300,900,3600]; host): Shelving durations offered, in seconds.\nsize (array; default [640,240]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; derived): Alarms {id, timestamp, source, priority, message, state, shelved_until, suppressed, out_of_service}. Written by the host (Python: raise_alarm(), suppress(), ...); without a host owning the state, the front end applies acknowledgements, shelving and its expiry, and writes the list back (HOST-004, HOST-012).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.AlarmList"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.AnalogIndicator","page":"API reference","text":"AnalogIndicator(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nAnalogIndicator(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA AnalogIndicator widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"analogindicator\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nnormal_hi (number or nothing; default null; host): Upper end of the normal operating range.\nnormal_lo (number or nothing; default null; host): Lower end of the normal operating range, shaded on the scale (IND-002).\norientation (\"horizontal\", \"vertical\"; default \"horizontal\"; host): Bar direction.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default true; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [240,56]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels. The Python class uses (70, 220) when created vertical; other hosts give the size with the orientation.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntarget (number or nothing; default null; host): Desired value, marked on the scale.\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.AnalogIndicator"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Annunciator","page":"API reference","text":"Annunciator(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Annunciator widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"annunciator\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ncolumns (integer; default 4; host): Windows per row.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nfirst_out (boolean; default false; host): Mark the first window to alarm until reset (IND-042).\nhorn (boolean; default false; derived): True while an alert or ringback is not silenced (no sound is played). Derived.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsequence (\"A\", \"M\", \"R\"; default \"A\"; host): ISA-18.1 sequence: A automatic reset, M manual reset, R ringback. Changing it restarts every window (active: alert, else normal).\nsize (array; default [420,170]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntest (boolean; default false; host and operator): Lamp test, while the TEST button is held.\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; derived): Windows {tag, text, color, active, state, first}. The host sets the process condition (active). The states, the first-out mark and the horn are derived through the sequence and the operator actions: by the host when it owns the state (Python: set(), acknowledge(), ...), otherwise by the front end, which writes them back (HOST-004).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Annunciator"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.BarGraph","page":"API reference","text":"BarGraph(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nBarGraph(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA BarGraph widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"bargraph\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_levels (array; default []; derived): Alarm level of each bar (a bar without a value is normal). Derived: by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end (HOST-004).\nbars (array; default []; host): Bars: a label, or {label, normal_lo, normal_hi, lolo, lo, hi, hihi}; only label is required, missing limits are null.\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis of the bar alarm levels (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host)\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the shared scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the shared scale.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [260,160]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (array; default []; host): One value per bar.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.BarGraph"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.BitField","page":"API reference","text":"BitField(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nBitField(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA BitField widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"bitfield\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nbits (8, 16, 32; default 16; host): Word size.\ncolors (array; default []; host): CSS on color of each bit, bit 0 first; empty or missing: on_color.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlabels (array; default []; host): Label of each bit, bit 0 first; a bit without a label is shown dimmed.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nmsb_first (boolean; default true; host): Draw the most significant bit on the left, as the word is written.\non_color (string; default \"#22c55e\"; host): CSS color of a set bit.\nshow_hex (boolean; default true; host): Also show the word in hexadecimal.\nsize (array; default [520,76]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (integer; default 0; host and operator): The word; bit 0 is the least significant bit. Must be below 2**bits (Python rejects larger values; the front end shows only the bits of the word). Set by the host, or by the user toggling a bit in control mode (IND-112).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.BitField"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Compass","page":"API reference","text":"Compass(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nCompass(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Compass widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"compass\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.0f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 360; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [160,160]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 8; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"°\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Heading in degrees, wrapped into [0, 360) (a finite value v is stored as v modulo 360, with a positive result).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Compass"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.DeviationIndicator","page":"API reference","text":"DeviationIndicator(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nDeviationIndicator(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA DeviationIndicator widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"deviation\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nformat (string; default \"%.2f\"; host): printf-like spec of the deviation (NUM-004).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsetpoint (number; default 0; host): Setpoint; the bar shows value - setpoint.\nsize (array; default [220,44]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nspan (number; default 10; host): Half-range of the bar (must be > 0).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntolerance (number; default 1; host): Half-width of the tolerance band; outside it the bar takes the alarm color and reads HIGH or LOW.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host): Unit shown with the deviation.\nvalue (number; default \"nan\"; host): Measured value.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.DeviationIndicator"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Dial","page":"API reference","text":"Dial(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nDial(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Dial widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"dial\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nangle_range (number; default 300; host): Angle swept by one turn of the scale, in degrees.\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [160,160]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nturns (integer; default 1; host): Number of turns for the full scale (multi-turn dial, e.g. a ten-turn potentiometer).\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Dial"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.DigitalWaveformGraph","page":"API reference","text":"DigitalWaveformGraph(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA DigitalWaveformGraph widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"digitalgraph\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nannotations (array; default []; host): Text annotations {x, y, text, color} in data coordinates (CHART-105).\nbuses (array; default []; host): Groups of lines {name, lines} shown as one hexadecimal value (first listed line = MSB). Python rejects buses naming a missing line; the front end ignores such lines.\ncursor_values (array; default []; host): Readout of the cursors for the host program, {name, x, values}, computed by the host from its data. The front end draws its own readout and does not read this trait.\ncursors (array; default []; host and operator): Cursors {x, name, color} (CHART-104). Dragged or typed by the operator, also on indicators; a host may complete a missing name as C&lt;n> (Python does).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\ndt (number; default 1; host): Sample interval in x-axis units; 0 is shown as 1.\nexport (boolean; default true; host): Offer CSV, PNG and SVG downloads in the toolbar (CHART-107).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlines (array; default []; host): Line names; a missing name is shown as D&lt;k>. Python names the lines D0, D1, ... when their number changes.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nshow_lines_in_bus (boolean; default true; host): Also draw the lines of each bus under it.\nsize (array; default [480,240]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (object; default {}; host): Size of the data {n_samples, n_lines}, written by the host with each data message.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nx0 (number; default 0; host): x-axis position of the first sample.\nx_unit (string; default \"\"; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.DigitalWaveformGraph"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.EmergencyStop","page":"API reference","text":"EmergencyStop(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nEmergencyStop(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA EmergencyStop widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"emergencystop\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_pressed (boolean; default false; front end): True while the pointer (or Space / Enter) is held on the control.\n_seq (integer; default 0; front end): Sequence number of the last press / release update sent by the front end; a host drops an update whose number is not newer (BOOL-010).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nconfirm (boolean; default false; host): Ask for a confirmation before changing the value (BOOL-011).\ndefault_state (boolean; default false; host): State a latch returns to once the host has read it (BOOL-008).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlatch_timeout (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which an unread latch expires (host side); 0: never.\nmechanical_action (\"switch_when_pressed\"; default \"switch_when_pressed\"; host): Only switch_when_pressed: a press latches the stop.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [110,110]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host and operator): True once pressed. The front end only ever writes true; only the host resets it to false (Python: reset()). A Python kernel refuses false from any other source.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.EmergencyStop"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.EquipmentTree","page":"API reference","text":"EquipmentTree(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nEquipmentTree(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA EquipmentTree widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"equipmenttree\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nexpanded (array; default []; host and operator): Ids of the expanded nodes. Set by the host, or by the operator expanding and collapsing nodes.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nnodes (array; default []; host): Root nodes, each {label, id, level, status, children}. Python rejects a node without a label, an unknown status or a repeated id; without a kernel such a node (and its children) is skipped.\nshow_level (boolean; default true; host): Show the level of each node next to its label.\nsize (array; default [320,280]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (string; default \"\"; host and operator): Id of the selected node, empty for none. Set by the host, or by the operator selecting a node in control mode.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.EquipmentTree"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.EventLog","page":"API reference","text":"EventLog(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA EventLog widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"eventlog\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmax_events (integer; default 500; host): Number of events kept (the oldest are dropped).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [600,200]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; host): Events in chronological order, {id, time, source, category, message}. Written by the host (Python: log(), connect()); the view shows at most the newest max_events.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.EventLog"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.FillSlide","page":"API reference","text":"FillSlide(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nFillSlide(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA FillSlide widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"fillslide\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nfill_color (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color of the filled part; empty: the theme color. Unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\norientation (\"horizontal\", \"vertical\"; default \"horizontal\"; host): Track direction.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [260,70]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels. The Python class uses (80, 240) when created vertical; other hosts give the size with the orientation.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.FillSlide"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Gauge","page":"API reference","text":"Gauge(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nGauge(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Gauge widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"gauge\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npeak (number or nothing; default null; derived): Held peak, null when none. Derived from the history of value (time dependent): by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end (HOST-004).\npeak_decay (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which the held peak is released at the next value; 0: held until reset.\npeak_hold (boolean; default false; host): Track and show the highest value (NUM-110).\nranges (array; default []; host): Colored ranges drawn on the scale; unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nsetpoint (number or nothing; default null; host): Setpoint drawn as a second, dashed pointer with a hollow marker, and stated in the text alternative; null: none (IND-116).\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [160,160]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvariant (\"circular\", \"semicircular\"; default \"circular\"; host)\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Gauge"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.IntensityChart","page":"API reference","text":"IntensityChart(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA IntensityChart widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"intensitychart\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nannotations (array; default []; host): Text annotations {x, y, text, color} in data coordinates (CHART-105).\nautoscale_z (boolean; default true; host)\ncolormap (\"viridis\", \"inferno\", \"magma\", \"plasma\", \"gray\", \"jet\"; default \"viridis\"; host)\ncursor_values (array; default []; host): Readout of the cursors for the host program, {name, x, values}, computed by the host from its data. The front end draws its own readout and does not read this trait.\ncursors (array; default []; host and operator): Cursors {x, name, color} (CHART-104). Dragged or typed by the operator, also on indicators; a host may complete a missing name as C&lt;n> (Python does).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\ndt (number; default 1; host): Time step between rows in x-axis units; 0 is shown as 1.\nexport (boolean; default true; host): Offer CSV, PNG and SVG downloads in the toolbar (CHART-107).\nhistory (integer; default 200; host): Rows kept and shown.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nn_bins (integer; default 64; host): Values per row.\nshow_colorbar (boolean; default true; host)\nsize (array; default [480,240]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (object; default {}; host): Summary of the latest row {rows, min, max, argmax}, written by the host with each append.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nx_unit (string; default \"\"; host)\ny_max (number or nothing; default null; host): Value of the upper edge of the last bin; null: y_min + n_bins.\ny_min (number; default 0; host): Value of the lower edge of the first bin.\nz_max (number; default 1; host)\nz_min (number; default 0; host): Color range when autoscale_z is off.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.IntensityChart"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.KPITile","page":"API reference","text":"KPITile(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nKPITile(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA KPITile widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"kpitile\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host)\nhigher_is_better (boolean; default true; host): Which side of the target is good (shown with ✓ / ✗).\nhistory (integer; default 30; host): Number of values kept for the sparkline.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nshow_sparkline (boolean; default true; host): Draw the history as a sparkline.\nsize (array; default [190,96]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntarget (number or nothing; default null; host): Target; null: no difference shown.\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (number; default \"nan\"; host): Current value of the indicator.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.KPITile"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Knob","page":"API reference","text":"Knob(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nKnob(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Knob widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"knob\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nangle_range (number; default 270; host): Angle swept by the scale, in degrees.\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [160,160]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Knob"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.LED","page":"API reference","text":"LED(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nLED(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA LED widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"led\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_pressed (boolean; default false; front end): True while the pointer (or Space / Enter) is held on the control.\n_seq (integer; default 0; front end): Sequence number of the last press / release update sent by the front end; a host drops an update whose number is not newer (BOOL-010).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nblink (boolean; default false; host): Blink while on (steady outline when reduced motion is requested, A11Y-005).\nblink_hz (number; default 2; host): Blink frequency in Hz.\nconfirm (boolean; default false; host): Ask for a confirmation before changing the value (BOOL-011).\ndefault_state (boolean; default false; host): State a latch returns to once the host has read it (BOOL-008).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlatch_timeout (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which an unread latch expires (host side); 0: never.\nmechanical_action (\"switch_when_pressed\", \"switch_when_released\", \"switch_until_released\", \"latch_when_pressed\", \"latch_when_released\", \"latch_until_released\"; default \"switch_when_pressed\"; host): How the control reacts to the pointer (BOOL-007). With a latch, the host reads the value and restores default_state; without a host that does it, a latched value stays set.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\noff_color (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color when off; empty: a dark version of on_color.\non_color (string; default \"#22c55e\"; host): CSS color when lit; unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\nshape (\"round\", \"square\"; default \"round\"; host): LED shape (the state is also given by text for assistive technologies, A11Y-003).\nsize (array; default [48,48]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host and operator): State of the control or indicator. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.LED"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Meter","page":"API reference","text":"Meter(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nMeter(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Meter widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"meter\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nangle_range (number; default 90; host): Angle swept by the scale, in degrees.\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npeak (number or nothing; default null; derived): Held peak, null when none. Derived from the history of value (time dependent): by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end (HOST-004).\npeak_decay (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which the held peak is released at the next value; 0: held until reset.\npeak_hold (boolean; default false; host): Track and show the highest value (NUM-110).\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nsetpoint (number or nothing; default null; host): Setpoint drawn as a second, dashed pointer with a hollow marker, and stated in the text alternative; null: none (IND-116).\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [200,140]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Meter"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.MixedSignalGraph","page":"API reference","text":"MixedSignalGraph(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA MixedSignalGraph widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"mixedgraph\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nanalog_fraction (number; default 0.55; host): Share of the height given to the analog traces.\nannotations (array; default []; host): Text annotations {x, y, text, color} in data coordinates (CHART-105).\nbuses (array; default []; host): Groups of lines {name, lines} shown as one hexadecimal value (first listed line = MSB). Python rejects buses naming a missing line; the front end ignores such lines.\ncursor_values (array; default []; host): Readout of the cursors for the host program, {name, x, values}, computed by the host from its data. The front end draws its own readout and does not read this trait.\ncursors (array; default []; host and operator): Cursors {x, name, color} (CHART-104). Dragged or typed by the operator, also on indicators; a host may complete a missing name as C&lt;n> (Python does).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\ndt (number; default 1; host): Sample interval in x-axis units; 0 is shown as 1.\nexport (boolean; default true; host): Offer CSV, PNG and SVG downloads in the toolbar (CHART-107).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlines (array; default []; host): Line names; a missing name is shown as D&lt;k>. Python names the lines D0, D1, ... when their number changes.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nshow_lines_in_bus (boolean; default true; host): Also draw the lines of each bus under it.\nsize (array; default [520,320]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\ntraces (array; default []; host): Optional style of each analog trace {name, color, width, visible}.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (object; default {}; host): Size of the data {n_samples, n_lines}, written by the host with each data message.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nx0 (number; default 0; host): x-axis position of the first sample.\nx_unit (string; default \"\"; host)\ny_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\ny_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Analog y range; null (either limit): scaled to the data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.MixedSignalGraph"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Motor","page":"API reference","text":"Motor(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nMotor(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Motor widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"motor\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nanimate (boolean; default true; host): Animate while turning (off when reduced motion is requested).\nauto (boolean; default true; host and operator): Automatic mode: the commands are disabled on the faceplate. The faceplate AUTO / MANUAL buttons send auto and manual commands; without a host owning the state, the front end applies them itself (HOST-012).\ncommands (array; default [\"forward\",\"reverse\",\"stop\"]; host): Commands offered on the faceplate (a constant of each widget).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsimulate (boolean; default false; host): A command sets the state itself (teaching, simulations): see the x-awi-simulated table of commands. Applied by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end.\nsize (array; default [90,90]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntag (string; default \"\"; host): Instrument tag shown on the faceplate (e.g. P-101).\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (\"stopped\", \"forward\", \"reverse\", \"fault\"; default \"stopped\"; host): Motor state (feedback from the process).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Motor"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.NumericEntry","page":"API reference","text":"NumericEntry(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nNumericEntry(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA NumericEntry widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"numericentry\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\nconfirm_delta (number or nothing; default null; host): A change larger than this asks for a second Enter (confirmation); null: no confirmation (IND-104).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.2f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [180,230]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.NumericEntry"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.PIDFaceplate","page":"API reference","text":"PIDFaceplate(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA PIDFaceplate widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"pidfaceplate\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of pv. Derived: by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end (HOST-004).\nconfirm_delta (number or nothing; default null; host): A change of SP or OP larger than this needs a confirmation (IND-032); null: never.\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Alarm hysteresis (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec of the values (NUM-004).\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit on PV.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit on PV.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit on PV.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit on PV.\nloop_mode (\"MAN\", \"AUTO\", \"CAS\"; default \"AUTO\"; host): Loop mode: MAN (operator sets OP), AUTO (operator sets SP), CAS (neither). Must be one of modes.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nmodes (array; default [\"MAN\",\"AUTO\"]; host): Modes offered on the faceplate.\nop (number; default 0; host): Output, clamped to op_min .. op_max. Changed by the operator in MAN.\nop_max (number; default 100; host): Upper output limit.\nop_min (number; default 0; host): Lower output limit.\nop_unit (string; default \"%\"; host): Unit of OP.\npv (number; default \"nan\"; host): Process value (measurement), set by the host.\npv_max (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the PV scale.\npv_min (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the PV scale.\nsize (array; default [240,236]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nsp (number; default 0; host): Setpoint, clamped to sp_min .. sp_max (or the PV range). Changed by the operator in AUTO (IND-031).\nsp_max (number or nothing; default null; host): Upper setpoint limit; null: pv_max.\nsp_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Lower setpoint limit; null: pv_min.\nsp_tracking (boolean; default false; host): Leaving MAN sets SP to PV (bumpless transfer, IND-034).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntag (string; default \"\"; host): Loop tag, e.g. TIC-101.\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host): Unit of PV and SP.\nvalue (object; default {}; derived): Summary {pv, sp, op, mode}. Derived: by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.PIDFaceplate"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.PictureControl","page":"API reference","text":"PictureControl(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA PictureControl widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"picture\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nbackground (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color of the background; empty: transparent.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [320,200]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (object; default {}; derived): Last click {x, y, button} in CSS pixels from the top-left corner (SPEC-006), control mode only. Written by the host when it owns the state; without one, the front end writes it back (HOST-012). The click is always sent as a click message.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.PictureControl"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Pipe","page":"API reference","text":"Pipe(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nPipe(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Pipe widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"pipe\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nflow_animation (boolean; default true; host): Animate a moving pattern while flowing (off when reduced motion is requested).\nflow_direction (\"forward\", \"reverse\"; default \"forward\"; host): Direction of the moving pattern.\nfluid_color (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color of the fluid; unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nrotation (0, 90, 180, 270; default 0; host): Rotation in degrees.\nshape (\"straight\", \"elbow\", \"tee\", \"cross\"; default \"straight\"; host): Unrotated: straight left to right, elbow left to bottom, tee left to right with a branch to the bottom, cross all four sides.\nsize (array; default [80,80]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nthickness (number; default 14; host): Pipe thickness in pixels.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host): True while the fluid flows.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Pipe"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.PolarPlot","page":"API reference","text":"PolarPlot(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nPolarPlot(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA PolarPlot widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"polar\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nangle_unit (\"deg\", \"rad\"; default \"deg\"; host)\ndirection (\"ccw\", \"cw\"; default \"ccw\"; host): Positive sense of the angles.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nr_max (number or nothing; default null; host and operator): Radial range; null or not positive: scaled to the data. Set by the operator with the mouse wheel or the r max field (CHART-108).\nrings (integer; default 4; host): Approximate number of grid rings.\nshow_legend (boolean; default true; host)\nsize (array; default [260,260]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (array; default []; host): Data sets {name, color, style, r, theta}; r and theta have the same length.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nzero (\"E\", \"N\"; default \"E\"; host): Where angle 0 is: east (mathematical) or north (compass).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.PolarPlot"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Pump","page":"API reference","text":"Pump(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nPump(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Pump widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"pump\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nanimate (boolean; default true; host): Rotate while running (off when reduced motion is requested).\nauto (boolean; default true; host and operator): Automatic mode: the commands are disabled on the faceplate. The faceplate AUTO / MANUAL buttons send auto and manual commands; without a host owning the state, the front end applies them itself (HOST-012).\ncommands (array; default [\"start\",\"stop\"]; host): Commands offered on the faceplate (a constant of each widget).\ndirection (\"right\", \"left\", \"up\", \"down\"; default \"right\"; host): Discharge direction of the symbol.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsimulate (boolean; default false; host): A command sets the state itself (teaching, simulations): see the x-awi-simulated table of commands. Applied by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end.\nsize (array; default [90,90]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntag (string; default \"\"; host): Instrument tag shown on the faceplate (e.g. P-101).\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (\"stopped\", \"running\", \"fault\"; default \"stopped\"; host): Pump state (feedback from the process).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Pump"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.PushButton","page":"API reference","text":"PushButton(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nPushButton(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA PushButton widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"pushbutton\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_pressed (boolean; default false; front end): True while the pointer (or Space / Enter) is held on the control.\n_seq (integer; default 0; front end): Sequence number of the last press / release update sent by the front end; a host drops an update whose number is not newer (BOOL-010).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ncolor (\"grey\", \"green\", \"red\", \"black\", \"yellow\", \"blue\", \"white\"; default \"grey\"; host): Cap color (IEC 60073: green to start, red to stop...).\nconfirm (boolean; default false; host): Ask for a confirmation before changing the value (BOOL-011).\ndefault_state (boolean; default false; host): State a latch returns to once the host has read it (BOOL-008).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlamp (boolean or nothing; default null; host): Built-in lamp: true lit, false unlit, null no lamp (BOOL-015). Feedback set by the host, independent of value.\nlamp_blink (boolean; default false; host): Flash the lamp.\nlamp_color (\"green\", \"red\", \"amber\", \"blue\", \"white\"; default \"green\"; host): Lamp color.\nlatch_timeout (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which an unread latch expires (host side); 0: never.\nmechanical_action (\"switch_when_pressed\", \"switch_when_released\", \"switch_until_released\", \"latch_when_pressed\", \"latch_when_released\", \"latch_until_released\"; default \"latch_when_released\"; host): How the control reacts to the pointer (BOOL-007). With a latch, the host reads the value and restores default_state; without a host that does it, a latched value stays set.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nshape (\"rect\", \"round\"; default \"rect\"; host): rect (panel button) or round (operator); the Python class uses a 90 x 90 size for round.\nsize (array; default [110,44]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntext (string; default \"OK\"; host): Caption (plain text, SEC-002).\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host and operator): State of the control or indicator. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.PushButton"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.RadarChart","page":"API reference","text":"RadarChart(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nRadarChart(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA RadarChart widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"radar\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\naxes (array; default []; host): Axis names; empty: axes numbered from the longest data set.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nfill (boolean; default true; host): Fill the data set polygons.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nranges (array; default []; host): [min, max] per axis, max > min; an axis without a valid range goes from 0 to the largest value of the data sets.\nshow_legend (boolean; default true; host)\nsize (array; default [260,260]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; host): Data sets {name, color, values}.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.RadarChart"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.RecipeTable","page":"API reference","text":"RecipeTable(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nRecipeTable(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA RecipeTable widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"recipetable\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ncolumns (array; default []; host): Columns {name, title, type, unit, min, max, step, format, choices, readonly, default}. Python normalizes them (a string is a number column of that name, missing keys get their defaults) and rejects duplicate names, unknown keys, max &lt; min and choice columns without choices.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmax_rows (integer; default 100; host): Most rows the table may hold.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nrow_edit (boolean; default false; host): Let the operator add and delete rows (IND-114).\nsize (array; default [560,220]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; host and operator): Rows, each a dict keyed by column name, every cell valid for its column. Written by the host (Python checks every row); operator edits arrive as messages and are applied by the host, or by the front end when no host owns the state (HOST-012).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.RecipeTable"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.RockerSwitch","page":"API reference","text":"RockerSwitch(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nRockerSwitch(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA RockerSwitch widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"rockerswitch\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_pressed (boolean; default false; front end): True while the pointer (or Space / Enter) is held on the control.\n_seq (integer; default 0; front end): Sequence number of the last press / release update sent by the front end; a host drops an update whose number is not newer (BOOL-010).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nconfirm (boolean; default false; host): Ask for a confirmation before changing the value (BOOL-011).\ndefault_state (boolean; default false; host): State a latch returns to once the host has read it (BOOL-008).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlatch_timeout (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which an unread latch expires (host side); 0: never.\nmechanical_action (\"switch_when_pressed\", \"switch_when_released\", \"switch_until_released\", \"latch_when_pressed\", \"latch_when_released\", \"latch_until_released\"; default \"switch_when_pressed\"; host): How the control reacts to the pointer (BOOL-007). With a latch, the host reads the value and restores default_state; without a host that does it, a latched value stays set.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [60,100]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host and operator): State of the control or indicator. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.RockerSwitch"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.SelectorSwitch","page":"API reference","text":"SelectorSwitch(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nSelectorSwitch(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA SelectorSwitch widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"selectorswitch\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndefault_position (string or nothing; default null; host): Position the switch returns to from a spring-return position; also the resolved value. Ignored when not one of positions.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nkeyed (boolean; default false; host): Key switch: with locked, the front end cannot move it (IND-012).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlocked (boolean; default false; host): Key removed: the position is locked for the operator (the host can still set it).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npositions (array; default [\"HAND\",\"OFF\",\"AUTO\"]; host): 2 to 5 distinct position labels, left to right.\nsize (array; default [140,130]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nspring_return (array; default []; host): Positions that go back to default_position when the operator releases the switch (IND-013).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (string; default \"\"; host and operator): Label of the selected position. Empty, or not one of positions: default_position, else the middle position (the Python class resolves it when the widget is created).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.SelectorSwitch"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.SevenSegment","page":"API reference","text":"SevenSegment(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nSevenSegment(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA SevenSegment widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"sevensegment\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ncolor (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color of the lit segments; empty: the theme color. Unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndecimals (integer; default 1; host): Digits after the decimal point.\ndigits (integer; default 4; host): Number of digit positions.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 1000000000; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default -1000000000; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [200,80]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.SevenSegment"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.SlideSwitch","page":"API reference","text":"SlideSwitch(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nSlideSwitch(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA SlideSwitch widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"slideswitch\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_pressed (boolean; default false; front end): True while the pointer (or Space / Enter) is held on the control.\n_seq (integer; default 0; front end): Sequence number of the last press / release update sent by the front end; a host drops an update whose number is not newer (BOOL-010).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nconfirm (boolean; default false; host): Ask for a confirmation before changing the value (BOOL-011).\ndefault_state (boolean; default false; host): State a latch returns to once the host has read it (BOOL-008).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlatch_timeout (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which an unread latch expires (host side); 0: never.\nmechanical_action (\"switch_when_pressed\", \"switch_when_released\", \"switch_until_released\", \"latch_when_pressed\", \"latch_when_released\", \"latch_until_released\"; default \"switch_when_pressed\"; host): How the control reacts to the pointer (BOOL-007). With a latch, the host reads the value and restores default_state; without a host that does it, a latched value stays set.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [90,44]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host and operator): State of the control or indicator. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.SlideSwitch"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.SmithChart","page":"API reference","text":"SmithChart(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nSmithChart(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA SmithChart widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"smith\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nshow_admittance (boolean; default false; host): Also draw the constant-conductance circles.\nshow_legend (boolean; default true; host)\nsize (array; default [260,260]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; host): Data sets {name, color, style, re, im} of reflection coefficients Γ = (Z - z0) / (Z + z0); a host plotting impedances converts them (Python: plot(z, kind=\"impedance\")).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nz0 (number; default 50; host): Reference impedance in ohms, used to show impedances in the tooltips (must be > 0).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.SmithChart"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Sparkline","page":"API reference","text":"Sparkline(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Sparkline widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"sparkline\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nformat (string; default \"%.4g\"; host): printf-like spec of the last value (NUM-004).\nhistory (integer; default 60; host): Number of values kept and drawn.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [160,36]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (number; default \"nan\"; host): Last appended value, written by the host with each append (the view shows the newest value of its history when it has one).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Sparkline"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.StackLight","page":"API reference","text":"StackLight(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nStackLight(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA StackLight widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"stacklight\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nbuzzer (boolean; default false; host): Show a sounding buzzer indicator (no sound is played).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlabels (array; default []; host): Meaning of each tier, shown as text (A11Y-003).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [120,200]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntiers (array; default [\"red\",\"amber\",\"green\"]; host): Tier colors from top to bottom.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (array; default []; host): State of each tier. Resolved to one state per tier: missing states are off, extra ones ignored, an unknown state reads as off (the Python class pads or cuts the list when the tiers change).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.StackLight"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.StateMachine","page":"API reference","text":"StateMachine(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA StateMachine widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"statemachine\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\navailable_commands (array; default []; derived): Commands valid in the current state (IND-061). Derived from machine and value.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlast_command (string; default \"\"; derived): Last command applied.\nmachine (object; default {\"commands\":[\"Start\",\"Stop\",\"Hold\",\"Unhold\",\"Suspend\",\"Unsuspend\",\"Reset\",\"Abort\",\"Clear\"],\"initial\":\"Stopped\",\"routes\":{\"Clearing>Stopped\":[[2.5,3.85],[0.5,3.85]],\"Complete>Resetting\":[[4.5,2.8],[0.3,2.8]],\"Execute>Holding\":[[2.8,1],[3.5,1]],\"Execute>Suspending\":[[2.8,2],[3.5,2]],\"Unholding>Execute\":[[1.5,1],[2.2,1]],\"Unsuspending>Execute\":[[1.5,2],[2.2,2]]},\"states\":[{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Unholding\",\"x\":1,\"y\":0},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Held\",\"x\":2,\"y\":0},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Holding\",\"x\":3,\"y\":0},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Idle\",\"x\":0,\"y\":1},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Starting\",\"x\":1,\"y\":1},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Execute\",\"x\":2,\"y\":1},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Completing\",\"x\":3,\"y\":1},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Complete\",\"x\":4,\"y\":1},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Resetting\",\"x\":0,\"y\":2},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Unsuspending\",\"x\":1,\"y\":2},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Suspended\",\"x\":2,\"y\":2},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Suspending\",\"x\":3,\"y\":2},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Stopped\",\"x\":0,\"y\":3},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Stopping\",\"x\":1,\"y\":3},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Clearing\",\"x\":2,\"y\":3},{\"acting\":false,\"name\":\"Aborted\",\"x\":3,\"y\":3},{\"acting\":true,\"name\":\"Aborting\",\"x\":4,\"y\":3}],\"transitions\":[[\"Stopped\",\"Reset\",\"Resetting\"],[\"Resetting\",\"SC\",\"Idle\"],[\"Idle\",\"Start\",\"Starting\"],[\"Starting\",\"SC\",\"Execute\"],[\"Execute\",\"SC\",\"Completing\"],[\"Completing\",\"SC\",\"Complete\"],[\"Complete\",\"Reset\",\"Resetting\"],[\"Execute\",\"Hold\",\"Holding\"],[\"Holding\",\"SC\",\"Held\"],[\"Held\",\"Unhold\",\"Unholding\"],[\"Unholding\",\"SC\",\"Execute\"],[\"Execute\",\"Suspend\",\"Suspending\"],[\"Suspending\",\"SC\",\"Suspended\"],[\"Suspended\",\"Unsuspend\",\"Unsuspending\"],[\"Unsuspending\",\"SC\",\"Execute\"],[\"Stopping\",\"SC\",\"Stopped\"],[\"Aborting\",\"SC\",\"Aborted\"],[\"Aborted\",\"Clear\",\"Clearing\"],[\"Clearing\",\"SC\",\"Stopped\"],[\"Unholding\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Unholding\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Held\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Held\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Holding\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Holding\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Idle\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Idle\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Starting\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Starting\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Execute\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Execute\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Completing\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Completing\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Complete\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Complete\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Resetting\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Resetting\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Unsuspending\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Unsuspending\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Suspended\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Suspended\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Suspending\",\"Stop\",\"Stopping\"],[\"Suspending\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Stopped\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Stopping\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"],[\"Clearing\",\"Abort\",\"Aborting\"]],\"zones\":[{\"commands\":[\"Abort\"],\"rects\":[[0,0,5,3],[0,3,3,4]],\"shade\":true},{\"commands\":[\"Stop\"],\"rects\":[[0,0,5,3]]}]}; host): State model: {states: [{name, x, y, acting, title, group}], transitions: [[from, command, to]], commands, initial, global_commands, zones, routes}; the command SC completes an acting state (a host event). Missing positions, acting flags, commands and initial state are completed as the kernel does; an invalid model reads as this default (PackML).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nsize (array; default [720,380]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (string; default \"\"; derived): Current state. Empty or unknown: the initial state of the model. Written by the host, or by the front end when it applies an operator command without a host (HOST-012).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.StateMachine"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.SvgPanel","page":"API reference","text":"SvgPanel(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nSvgPanel(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA SvgPanel widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"svgpanel\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nproblems (array; default []; host): Elements with an unknown role or an invalid option, as '&lt;element>: &lt;reason>' (IND-125). Computed by Python; without a kernel the front end shows its own list.\nshow_entries (boolean; default true; host): Show an entry field for each value of a step control (IND-124).\nsize (array; default [400,300]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\nsvg (string; default \"\"; host): SVG document. Python sanitizes it; the front end sanitizes it again (no scripts, event handlers or external resources). A role is read from the data-awi attribute of an element, else from its inkscape:label attribute.\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (object; default {}; host and operator): Values of the bound names: numbers, texts, Booleans or null (shown as a dash). Written by the host, and by the operator through control roles in control mode; the kernel refuses a step value outside its limits.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.SvgPanel"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.SynopticCanvas","page":"API reference","text":"SynopticCanvas(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA SynopticCanvas widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"synoptic\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nbackground (bytes; default \"\"; host): PNG, JPEG or SVG image bytes; empty: none. A binary buffer in Jupyter; a host that only sends JSON may send base64 text. An SVG is shown through an image element: its scripts and external loads are disabled.\nbackground_mime (string; default \"\"; host): Type of the background: \"image/png\", \"image/jpeg\" or \"image/svg+xml\", set by Python from the bytes. When empty or another value, the front end detects the type from the bytes the same way.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nitems (array; default []; host): Widgets placed on the canvas {widget, x, y}. The children are rendered through the host widget manager (Jupyter, marimo); a host without one gets a placeholder per child, while the pipes and the background still render (HOST-009).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npipes (array; default []; host): Pipe runs {points, flow, direction, color, thickness} drawn by the canvas, with an optional flow animation.\nsize (array; default [640,360]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (object; default {}; host): Unused (always empty).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.SynopticCanvas"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Tank","page":"API reference","text":"Tank(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nTank(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Tank widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"tank\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nfill_color (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color of the liquid; empty: the theme color. Unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmarkers (array; default []; host): Level markers drawn on the tank, in scale units.\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [120,200]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Tank"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.ThemeSwitch","page":"API reference","text":"ThemeSwitch(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nThemeSwitch(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA ThemeSwitch widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"themeswitch\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npage_theme (boolean; default true; host): Also switch the notebook page theme where the host allows it (marimo).\nsize (array; default [240,30]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (\"auto\", \"light\", \"system\", \"dark\"; default \"auto\"; host and operator): Selected theme; auto until a position is chosen. With a Python kernel, every widget of the kernel follows it; other hosts apply the page theme only (STYLE-008).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.ThemeSwitch"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Thermometer","page":"API reference","text":"Thermometer(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nThermometer(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Thermometer widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"thermometer\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nfill_color (string; default \"\"; host): CSS color of the fluid column; empty: the theme color. Unsafe colors are ignored (SEC-002).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 120; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default -20; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [100,220]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 7; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"°C\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Thermometer"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.ToggleSwitch","page":"API reference","text":"ToggleSwitch(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nToggleSwitch(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA ToggleSwitch widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"toggleswitch\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_pressed (boolean; default false; front end): True while the pointer (or Space / Enter) is held on the control.\n_seq (integer; default 0; front end): Sequence number of the last press / release update sent by the front end; a host drops an update whose number is not newer (BOOL-010).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nconfirm (boolean; default false; host): Ask for a confirmation before changing the value (BOOL-011).\ndefault_state (boolean; default false; host): State a latch returns to once the host has read it (BOOL-008).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlatch_timeout (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which an unread latch expires (host side); 0: never.\nmechanical_action (\"switch_when_pressed\", \"switch_when_released\", \"switch_until_released\", \"latch_when_pressed\", \"latch_when_released\", \"latch_until_released\"; default \"switch_when_pressed\"; host): How the control reacts to the pointer (BOOL-007). With a latch, the host reads the value and restores default_state; without a host that does it, a latched value stays set.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\norientation (\"vertical\", \"horizontal\"; default \"vertical\"; host): Lever direction.\nsize (array; default [60,100]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels. The Python class uses (100, 60) when created horizontal; other hosts give the size with the orientation.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (boolean; default false; host and operator): State of the control or indicator. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.ToggleSwitch"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Transmitter","page":"API reference","text":"Transmitter(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nTransmitter(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Transmitter widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"transmitter\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.2f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [110,84]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstatus (\"ok\", \"failure\", \"check\", \"out_of_spec\", \"maintenance\"; default \"ok\"; host): Device status after the NAMUR NE 107 categories: ok, failure, check (function check), out_of_spec, maintenance (IND-081). While failure, the value is shown invalid (IND-082).\nstatus_text (string; default \"\"; host): Optional detail of the status, e.g. the diagnostic message.\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntag (string; default \"\"; host): Instrument tag, e.g. LT-101: function letters above the line, loop number below (IND-080).\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Transmitter"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.TrendChart","page":"API reference","text":"TrendChart(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA TrendChart widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"trendchart\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nannotations (array; default []; host): Text annotations {x, y, text, color} in data coordinates (CHART-105).\ncursor_values (array; default []; host): Readout of the cursors for the host program, {name, x, values}, computed by the host from its data. The front end draws its own readout and does not read this trait.\ncursors (array; default []; host and operator): Cursors {x, name, color} (CHART-104). Dragged or typed by the operator, also on indicators; a host may complete a missing name as C&lt;n> (Python does).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nexport (boolean; default true; host): Offer CSV, PNG and SVG downloads in the toolbar (CHART-107).\nhistory (integer; default 10000; host): Samples kept per pen (IND-074).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\npens (array; default []; host): Pens {name, unit, min, max, color, lolo, lo, hi, hihi, setpoint, format}. Python normalizes them (a string is a pen name, missing keys get their defaults) and rejects duplicate names, unknown keys and max &lt;= min; the front end shows an invalid scale as 0 .. 100.\nsize (array; default [560,260]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nspan (number; default 600; host and operator): Seconds shown; set by the operator with the span selector.\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (object; default {}; host): Latest value of each pen, by pen name, written by the host with each append.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nx_unit (string; default \"\"; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.TrendChart"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.VUMeter","page":"API reference","text":"VUMeter(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nVUMeter(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA VUMeter widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"vumeter\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nalarm_level (\"normal\", \"lo\", \"lolo\", \"hi\", \"hihi\"; default \"normal\"; derived): Alarm level of value (ALARM-002, ALARM-003). Derived: computed by the host when it owns the state (_session non-empty), otherwise by the front end, which writes it back (HOST-004).\nanimate (boolean; default false; host)\nanimation_ms (integer; default 200; host)\ncoerce (boolean; default false; host): Clamp values to [min, max] instead of rejecting typed values outside it (NUM-010).\ndeadband (number; default 0; host): Hysteresis: a level is left only when the value is back past its limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\neng_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\neng_min (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nentry (boolean; default true; host): Editable value field in control mode (API-014).\nformat (string; default \"%.1f\"; host): printf-like spec: %.2f, %.3e, %.3g, %.3n (engineering), %.3s (SI prefix) (NUM-004); %X, %x, %b, %o show the value as a hexadecimal, binary or octal integer, with an optional width padded with zeros such as %04X (IND-110), and values are then typed in that base.\nhi (number or nothing; default null; host): High alarm limit.\nhihi (number or nothing; default null; host): High-high alarm limit.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nlo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low alarm limit.\nlolo (number or nothing; default null; host): Low-low alarm limit (ALARM-001).\nmax (number; default 100; host): Upper end of the scale.\nmin (number; default 0; host): Lower end of the scale; must be below max, and > 0 on a log scale.\nminor_ticks (integer; default 4; host): Minor subdivisions per major interval.\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\norientation (\"vertical\", \"horizontal\"; default \"vertical\"; host)\npeak (number or nothing; default null; derived): Held peak, null when none. Derived from the history of value (time dependent): by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end (HOST-004).\npeak_decay (number; default 0; host): Seconds after which the held peak is released at the next value; 0: held until reset.\npeak_hold (boolean; default false; host): Track and show the highest value (NUM-110).\nraw_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nraw_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Engineering scaling: raw reading at eng_min (UNIT-003). Used by the host API only.\nscale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host)\nsegments (integer; default 20; host): Number of segments.\nshow_limits (boolean; default false; host): Draw the alarm limits on the scale.\nsize (array; default [60,200]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstep (number; default 0; host): Values entered by the user snap to min + k * step; 0: no snapping (NUM-005).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\nticks (integer; default 5; host): Major scale intervals.\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_rate (number; default 30; host): Maximum rate of intermediate values sent while dragging, in Hz (NUM-009).\nvalue (number; default 0; host and operator): Current value. Set by the host, or by the user in control mode. Shown clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalue_labels (array; default []; host): Named values, sorted by value (IND-118): the scale shows the labels instead of numbers, the readout the label of the current value (within 1e-9 of the span), and the value field accepts a label (case ignored).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.VUMeter"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.Valve","page":"API reference","text":"Valve(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\nValve(value; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA Valve widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"valve\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nauto (boolean; default true; host and operator): Automatic mode: the commands are disabled on the faceplate. The faceplate AUTO / MANUAL buttons send auto and manual commands; without a host owning the state, the front end applies them itself (HOST-012).\ncommands (array; default [\"open\",\"close\"]; host): Commands offered on the faceplate (a constant of each widget).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"control\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\norientation (\"horizontal\", \"vertical\"; default \"horizontal\"; host)\nposition (number or nothing; default null; host): Opening in % for a control valve (feedback); null: on/off valve. A control valve faceplate also takes a position demand in manual mode (with simulate, applied to position and value).\nsimulate (boolean; default false; host): A command sets the state itself (teaching, simulations): see the x-awi-simulated table of commands. Applied by the host when it owns the state, otherwise by the front end.\nsize (array; default [90,90]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntag (string; default \"\"; host): Instrument tag shown on the faceplate (e.g. P-101).\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nvalue (\"open\", \"closed\", \"transit\", \"fault\"; default \"closed\"; host): Valve state (feedback from the process).\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.Valve"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.WaveformChart","page":"API reference","text":"WaveformChart(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA WaveformChart widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"waveformchart\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nannotations (array; default []; host): Text annotations {x, y, text, color} in data coordinates (CHART-105).\nautoscale_y (boolean; default false; host and operator)\nautoscale_y2 (boolean; default false; host)\ncursor_values (array; default []; host): Readout of the cursors for the host program, {name, x, values}, computed by the host from its data. The front end draws its own readout and does not read this trait.\ncursors (array; default []; host and operator): Cursors {x, name, color} (CHART-104). Dragged or typed by the operator, also on indicators; a host may complete a missing name as C&lt;n> (Python does).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\ndt (number; default 1; host): Sample interval in x-axis units; 0 is shown as 1.\nexport (boolean; default true; host): Offer CSV, PNG and SVG downloads in the toolbar (CHART-107).\nhistory (integer; default 1024; host): Points kept and shown per trace.\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nn_traces (integer; default 1; host)\npaused (boolean; default false; host): Freeze the display; samples keep arriving (CHART-009).\nshow_legend (boolean; default true; host)\nsize (array; default [480,240]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\ntraces (array; default []; host): Optional style of each trace {name, color, width, visible, axis}.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nupdate_mode (\"strip\", \"scope\", \"sweep\"; default \"strip\"; host): strip: continuous scroll; scope: fill then restart; sweep: a moving cursor overwrites the oldest data.\nvalue (array; default []; host): Latest sample of each trace, written by the host with each append.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nx_unit (string; default \"\"; host)\ny2_max (number; default 1; host)\ny2_min (number; default 0; host): Range of the secondary axis on the right, for the traces with axis right, when autoscale_y2 is off (IND-117).\ny2_unit (string; default \"\"; host): Unit of the secondary axis, shown under it and after the values of its traces under a cursor.\ny_max (number; default 1; host and operator)\ny_min (number; default -1; host and operator): Y range when autoscale_y is off; set by the operator with the axes panel.\ny_scale (\"linear\", \"log\"; default \"linear\"; host): Scale of the left Y axis; on a logarithmic axis values &lt;= 0 are not drawn, and a range reaching 0 or below starts at y_max / 1000 (IND-117).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.WaveformChart"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#AnywidgetInstruments.XYGraph","page":"API reference","text":"XYGraph(; id, traits...) -> Instrument\n\nA XYGraph widget of anywidget-instruments (kind \"xygraph\"). See instrument for the checks applied to the traits.\n\nTraits\n\n_heartbeat (number; default 0; host): Heartbeat period announced by the host, in seconds. 0 (default): no stale-data detection. With a non-empty _session and a period > 0, the host sends {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\": _session} every period (ROB-001, HOST-003).\n_session (string; default \"\"; host): Identity of the host session that owns the state. Non-empty: the host is authoritative for derived traits and may announce heartbeats (HOST-003, HOST-004). Empty (default): the front end computes derived traits itself.\nannotations (array; default []; host): Text annotations {x, y, text, color} in data coordinates (CHART-105).\ncursor_values (array; default []; host): Readout of the cursors for the host program, {name, x, values}, computed by the host from its data. The front end draws its own readout and does not read this trait.\ncursors (array; default []; host and operator): Cursors {x, name, color} (CHART-104). Dragged or typed by the operator, also on indicators; a host may complete a missing name as C&lt;n> (Python does).\ndisabled (boolean; default false; host): Greyed out, input rejected.\nexport (boolean; default true; host): Offer CSV, PNG and SVG downloads in the toolbar (CHART-107).\nlabel (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text, never interpreted as HTML (SEC-002).\nmode (\"control\", \"indicator\"; default \"indicator\"; host): \"control\": the user sets the value; \"indicator\": display only.\nseries (array; default []; host): Data sets {name, color, style, width}, drawn in order. A set whose data have not arrived is not drawn; data of a name not listed here are dropped.\nshow_legend (boolean; default true; host)\nsize (array; default [480,300]; host): [width, height] in CSS pixels.\nskin (object; default {}; host): Replaceable drawing parts: part name -> SVG source, sanitized (STYLE-005, STYLE-006).\nstyle (\"modern\", \"classic\", \"system\"; default \"modern\"; host)\ntheme (\"auto\", \"light\", \"dark\", \"system\"; default \"auto\"; host): \"auto\": the style decides; \"system\": the host page or the operating system (STYLE-007).\ntooltip (string; default \"\"; host): Plain text shown on hover.\nunit (string; default \"\"; host)\nvalue (object; default {}; host): Number of data sets and of points {sets, points}, written by the host with each data message.\nvisible (boolean; default true; host)\nx_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\nx_min (number or nothing; default null; host): X range; null: from the data.\nx_unit (string; default \"\"; host)\ny_max (number or nothing; default null; host): A number, or null when not set.\ny_min (number or nothing; default null; host): Y range; null: from the data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AnywidgetInstruments.XYGraph"},{"category":"section","location":"roadmap/#Roadmap","page":"Roadmap","text":"Development phases are milestones, numbered 0.0.x (phase 0 is 0.0.1); they are not releases.","title":"Roadmap"},{"category":"section","location":"roadmap/#Phase-0-—-0.0.1:-foundations-(done)","page":"Roadmap","text":"Vendored front end and trait contract of anywidget-instruments, with their origin and checksum.\nA constructor per widget class; traits checked against the contract.\nJSON encoding (non-finite numbers, bytes), binary buffers.\nMessages: heartbeat, TrendChart, Sparkline and KPITile data, a replaceable transport.\nShared rules: alarm levels, value coercion, scales, value labels, with the parity cases.\nStandalone HTML display and pages.\nKaimon Slate extension through SlateAFM, with a headless-validated example.","title":"Phase 0 — 0.0.1: foundations (done)"},{"category":"section","location":"roadmap/#Phase-1-—-0.0.2:-more-hosts","page":"Roadmap","text":"Bidirectional host for Bonito.jl (operator actions back to Julia).\nPluto.jl integration (@bind through AbstractPlutoDingetjes).\nHeartbeat helper (a task sending hb every _heartbeat seconds).","title":"Phase 1 — 0.0.2: more hosts"},{"category":"section","location":"roadmap/#Phase-2-—-0.0.3:-more-shared-rules","page":"Roadmap","text":"Julia ports of the other parity files: annunciator sequences, state machine transitions, PID faceplate, alarm list and banner, bar graphs, peak hold.\nMessage builders for WaveformChart, IntensityChart, XYGraph and the digital graphs.","title":"Phase 2 — 0.0.3: more shared rules"},{"category":"section","location":"roadmap/#Phase-3-—-0.0.4:-tooling","page":"Roadmap","text":"Registration in the General registry.\nAutomated refresh of the vendored front end when anywidget-instruments is released (a workflow opening a pull request).","title":"Phase 3 — 0.0.4: tooling"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#Specification","page":"Specification","text":"Requirements of AnywidgetInstruments.jl, written with the Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax (EARS) and prioritized with MoSCoW: Must, Should, Could, Won't (this time).\n\nThe widgets themselves (their traits, messages and behaviour) are specified by the anywidget-instruments specification; this package is a Julia host of their front end, following its trait contract for host authors (HOST-001 to HOST-012). Requirement IDs of that specification are quoted in parentheses where they apply.\n\nVersion Date Change\n0.1 2026-09-25 First version (phase 0, package 0.0.1)","title":"Specification"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#1.-General","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-GEN-001 M The package shall run on the current Julia release (1.13) and on the LTS release (1.10).\nJL-GEN-002 M The package shall not require Python, pip, Node.js or network access at run time.\nJL-GEN-003 M The package shall ship the front-end module (index.js), its styles (index.css), the flattened trait contract (contract.json) and the JSON Schemas of anywidget-instruments, unmodified except for the removed source map comment.\nJL-GEN-004 M The package shall record the version and the SHA-256 checksum of the wheel its front end was taken from (assets/SOURCE.toml).\nJL-GEN-005 M The core package shall depend only on JSON.jl and on standard libraries; integrations with notebook hosts shall be package extensions.\nJL-GEN-006 S The package shall keep the license notice of anywidget-instruments next to the vendored files.","title":"1. General"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#2.-Contract","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-CON-001 M The package shall expose the version of the vendored front end (frontend_version()).\nJL-CON-002 M The package shall list the concrete widget classes of the contract (widget_classes()), without the abstract bases.\nJL-CON-003 M The package shall give the trait specs of a widget class (trait_specs(class)) and its message specs (message_specs(class)).\nJL-CON-004 M When a class that is not in the contract is requested, the package shall throw an ArgumentError naming the class.\nJL-CON-005 S The package shall give the default traits of a class (default_traits(class)), non-finite defaults decoded.","title":"2. Contract"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#3.-Widgets","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-API-001 M The package shall provide a constructor for each concrete widget class of the contract, with the class name (Tank, Knob, …), taking traits as keyword arguments.\nJL-API-002 M Where a widget class has a value trait that is not read-only, its constructor shall accept the value as an optional first positional argument.\nJL-API-003 M The package shall provide instrument(class; traits...) building a widget from its class name given as a String or a Symbol.\nJL-API-004 M When a trait that the class does not declare is given, the package shall throw an ArgumentError naming the trait and the class.\nJL-API-005 M When a value that does not conform to the trait spec is given (type, enum values, exclusive bounds, tuple length, array length), the package shall throw an ArgumentError naming the trait.\nJL-API-006 M When a number outside the inclusive bounds of its spec is given, the package shall clamp it, as the front end does (HOST-002).\nJL-API-007 M The package shall convert conforming values to their JSON form: symbols to strings, tuples to arrays, integers of an integer trait to Int, numbers wrapped into [0, modulo).\nJL-API-008 M The package shall not store the _kind trait given by the user: it shall always be the kind of the class.\nJL-API-009 M The package shall let a widget be read and updated like a dictionary of traits (w[:value], w[:value] = x), with the same validation as the constructor.\nJL-API-010 M The package shall give the traits of a widget as a Dict{String,Any} of the traits set by the user and the kind (traits(w)), and all traits with defaults filled in (traits(w; defaults = true)).\nJL-API-011 S The package shall give each widget a message id (id keyword, default: a unique id), used by hosts to route custom messages.\nJL-API-012 S The package shall not export a constructor whose name is already exported by Base (for example Pipe); it shall stay reachable qualified.\nJL-API-013 C The package should provide update(w; traits...) returning a copy of w with some traits changed.\nJL-API-014 S The package shall update a plain trait dictionary (the bound value of a widget in a notebook host) with checked traits (merge_traits(d; traits...)), the class being found from its _kind.","title":"3. Widgets"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#4.-Encoding","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-ENC-001 M The package shall encode NaN and infinities of traits whose spec is nonfinite as the strings \"nan\", \"inf\" and \"-inf\", and decode those strings back to Float64.\nJL-ENC-002 M When a non-finite number is given to a trait whose spec is not nonfinite, the package shall throw an ArgumentError.\nJL-ENC-003 M The package shall serialize a widget to the JSON text of its traits (to_json(w)).\nJL-ENC-004 M The package shall encode a numeric array as the bytes of a buffer of a contract dtype (<f4, <f8, u1/uint8, …), little-endian whatever the host byte order (encode_buffer).\nJL-ENC-005 S The package shall accept a bytes trait given as a byte vector and store it as base64 text (HOST-010).","title":"4. Encoding"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#5.-Messages","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-MSG-001 M The package shall represent a custom message as its JSON content and its list of binary buffers (Message).\nJL-MSG-002 M The package shall build a heartbeat message {\"type\": \"hb\", \"session\", \"interval\"} (HOST-003).\nJL-MSG-003 M The package shall build append and snapshot messages of a TrendChart from the times and values of its pens, with one float64 time buffer and one float32 value buffer per pen entry.\nJL-MSG-004 S The package shall build the append message of a Sparkline and of a KPITile from their new values.\nJL-MSG-005 M When a message type is not declared host-to-front for the class of the widget, the package shall throw an ArgumentError.\nJL-MSG-006 M The package shall send messages through a replaceable transport (send_message(w, msg)); when no transport is installed, it shall throw an error telling how to install one.","title":"5. Messages"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#6.-Rules-shared-with-the-front-end","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-LOG-001 M The package shall compute alarm levels with hysteresis like the front end (alarm_level, ALARM-002, ALARM-003), and pass the shared cases of tests/parity/alarm_level.json.\nJL-LOG-002 M The package shall coerce values and check scales like the front end (coerce_value, valid_scale, NUM-006, NUM-010), and pass the shared cases of tests/parity/numeric.json.\nJL-LOG-003 S The package shall normalize value labels and look them up like the front end (normalize_value_labels, value_label_of, value_of_label, IND-118), and pass the shared cases of tests/parity/value_labels.json.\nJL-LOG-004 S When the host owns the state (non-empty _session), the package shall update alarm_level whenever the value or the limits of a widget with an alarm_level trait change (HOST-004).","title":"6. Rules shared with the front end"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#7.-Standalone-HTML","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-HTML-001 M The package shall render a widget as HTML (MIME\"text/html\") that loads the front-end module and runs it with a model held in the page, so that it displays in any environment showing HTML (Documenter, VS Code, Jupyter with IJulia, Pluto).\nJL-HTML-002 M The HTML shall embed the traits as JSON inside a <script type=\"application/json\"> element, escaped so that no trait value can close the element (SEC-002).\nJL-HTML-003 M By default the HTML shall be self-contained: the module and the styles are inlined once per page load.\nJL-HTML-004 S Where an asset base URL is set (set_asset_base!), the HTML shall load index.js and index.css from it instead of inlining them.\nJL-HTML-005 S The package shall render several widgets in one standalone HTML page (html_page(widgets...)), the module included once.\nJL-HTML-006 W The standalone HTML won't send operator actions back to Julia: it has no kernel.","title":"7. Standalone HTML"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#8.-KaimonSlate.jl","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-SLATE-001 M When SlateExtensionsBase is loaded, the package shall convert a widget to a Widget of the SlateAFM.AFM kind whose bound value is the trait dictionary and whose parameters are the module URL, the stylesheet URL and the message id.\nJL-SLATE-002 M When SlateExtensionsBase is loaded, the package shall serve its vendored front end from its __slate_frontend hook.\nJL-SLATE-003 S When SlateAFM is loaded, the package shall install a transport sending messages with SlateAFM.afm_emit.\nJL-SLATE-004 W The package won't register its own widget kind: rendering relies on the host shim of SlateAFM.","title":"8. KaimonSlate.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#9.-Quality","page":"Specification","text":"ID P Requirement\nJL-QA-001 M Every requirement marked M shall be covered by a test item (TestItemRunner.jl).\nJL-QA-002 M The package shall pass Aqua.jl checks.\nJL-QA-003 M The documentation shall build without warnings and publish llms.txt and llms-full.txt.\nJL-QA-004 S The package shall be formatted with JuliaFormatter (.JuliaFormatter.toml).","title":"9. Quality"},{"category":"section","location":"specification/#Out-of-scope-for-now","page":"Specification","text":"Bonito.jl / Pluto.jl bidirectional hosts (JL-HTML-006): a later phase.\nJulia ports of the other shared rules (annunciator sequences, state machine transitions, PID faceplate, …): later phases, one parity file at a time.","title":"Out of scope for now"},{"category":"section","location":"getting-started/#Getting-started","page":"Getting started","text":"","title":"Getting started"},{"category":"section","location":"getting-started/#Installation","page":"Getting started","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(url = \"https://github.com/s-celles/AnywidgetInstruments.jl\")\n\nThe package runs on Julia 1.10 (LTS) and later. It needs neither Python nor Node.js: the front end of anywidget-instruments is shipped with it (AnywidgetInstruments.assets_dir()), and assets/SOURCE.toml records the version and the checksum of the wheel it comes from.\n\nusing AnywidgetInstruments\nfrontend_version()\n\"0.1.0.dev0\"","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"getting-started/#Building-widgets","page":"Getting started","text":"Each widget class of anywidget-instruments has a constructor of the same name. Traits are keyword arguments; a widget with a writable value also takes it as the first argument:\n\nlevel = Tank(3.2; max = 4, unit = \"m\", hi = 3, show_limits = true, label = \"T-101\")\nTank (tank) id=\"awi-55b1b96c-df4a-4646-b976-29ec9ba04c91\"\n  hi = 3\n  label = \"T-101\"\n  max = 4\n  show_limits = true\n  unit = \"m\"\n  value = 3.2\n\ninstrument builds a widget from its class name, for example when the class comes from data:\n\ninstrument(:Knob, 2.5; max = 10, label = \"Gain\")\nKnob (knob) id=\"awi-1a9879e4-8b99-4997-a007-79110a9a4583\"\n  label = \"Gain\"\n  max = 10\n  value = 2.5\n\nA widget reads and writes like a dictionary. Unset traits read as their default:\n\nlevel[:value] = 2.0\nlevel[:value], level[:max], level[:mode]\n(2.0, 4, \"indicator\")","title":"Building widgets"},{"category":"section","location":"getting-started/#Checked-traits","page":"Getting started","text":"Every trait is checked against the trait contract:\n\nan unknown trait, or a value of the wrong type, throws an ArgumentError;\na number outside the inclusive bounds of its spec is clamped, as the front end does;\nsymbols become strings, tuples become arrays, a heading wraps into [0, 360).\n\ntry\n    Tank(; colour = \"red\")\ncatch err\n    sprint(showerror, err)\nend\n\"ArgumentError: Tank has no trait \\\"colour\\\"\"\n\nCompass(370)[:value]\n10.0\n\nThe trait specs themselves are available:\n\ntrait_specs(\"Tank\")[\"mode\"]\nDict{String, Any} with 5 entries:\n  \"type\"        => \"enum\"\n  \"values\"      => Any[\"control\", \"indicator\"]\n  \"description\" => \"\\\"control\\\": the user sets the value; \\\"indicator\\\": displa…\n  \"default\"     => \"indicator\"\n  \"writer\"      => \"host\"","title":"Checked traits"},{"category":"section","location":"getting-started/#Trait-dictionaries","page":"Getting started","text":"A host binds the front end to a plain dictionary of traits. traits(w) gives the traits that were set (and _kind), traits(w; defaults = true) every trait of the class, and to_json(w) the JSON text. NaN and infinities travel as the strings \"nan\", \"inf\" and \"-inf\":\n\ntraits(Tank(NaN; unit = \"m\"))\nDict{String, Any} with 3 entries:\n  \"unit\"  => \"m\"\n  \"_kind\" => \"tank\"\n  \"value\" => \"nan\"\n\nA notebook usually holds the bound dictionary rather than the widget: merge_traits updates it with the same checks, finding the class from _kind:\n\nmerge_traits(Dict(\"_kind\" => \"tank\", \"value\" => 1.0); value = 2.5, label = \"T-101\")\nDict{String, Any} with 3 entries:\n  \"label\" => \"T-101\"\n  \"_kind\" => \"tank\"\n  \"value\" => 2.5","title":"Trait dictionaries"},{"category":"section","location":"getting-started/#Displaying-widgets","page":"Getting started","text":"A widget has a text/html representation: it runs the front-end module in the page with a model holding its traits. It displays wherever HTML is shown: Documenter (as on these pages), VS Code, Jupyter with IJulia, Pluto. The operator can use the widget in the page, but there is no kernel: its actions do not come back to Julia (use Kaimon Slate for that).\n\nKnob(2.5; min = 0, max = 10, unit = \"dB\", label = \"Gain\")\nKnob (knob) id=\"awi-9ee2a076-6811-43ea-80fe-970b18d414ad\"\n  label = \"Gain\"\n  max = 10\n  min = 0\n  unit = \"dB\"\n  value = 2.5\n\nBy default each output is self-contained: the module and the styles are inlined (about 1 MB). Point the display at a copy of the assets to avoid it:\n\nAnywidgetInstruments.set_asset_base!(\"https://example.org/awi/\")   # serves index.js and index.css\n\nhtml_page writes several widgets into one standalone page, the module included once:\n\nhtml_page(\"station.html\", Tank(3.2; max = 4), Knob(2.5), LED(true); title = \"Station\")","title":"Displaying widgets"},{"category":"section","location":"widgets/#Widgets","page":"Widgets","text":"These widgets run live on this page: drag the knob, press the buttons. The behaviour of each widget is specified by anywidget-instruments; the traits of each class are listed in the API reference.","title":"Widgets"},{"category":"section","location":"widgets/#Numeric-controls-and-indicators","page":"Widgets","text":"Knob(2.5; min = 0, max = 10, step = 0.1, unit = \"dB\", label = \"Gain\")\nKnob (knob) id=\"awi-339d2adb-d8cb-4229-b1d4-94a19e34d695\"\n  label = \"Gain\"\n  max = 10\n  min = 0\n  step = 0.1\n  unit = \"dB\"\n  value = 2.5\n\nGauge(72.0; hi = 80, hihi = 90, show_limits = true, unit = \"bar\", label = \"Pressure\")\nGauge (gauge) id=\"awi-c6e6fb30-60dc-4b8f-ba1e-3e765b6779de\"\n  hi = 80\n  hihi = 90\n  label = \"Pressure\"\n  show_limits = true\n  unit = \"bar\"\n  value = 72.0\n\nThermometer(64.0; min = 0, max = 100, unit = \"°C\", hi = 85, show_limits = true, label = \"TT-101\")\nThermometer (thermometer) id=\"awi-51a5110d-2f22-4f5f-9f2f-33571bd67032\"\n  hi = 85\n  label = \"TT-101\"\n  max = 100\n  min = 0\n  show_limits = true\n  unit = \"°C\"\n  value = 64.0\n\nSevenSegment(1234.5; digits = 6, max = 10_000, label = \"Counter\")\nSevenSegment (sevensegment) id=\"awi-a008bef8-5f11-453c-b9db-a579e84c25a1\"\n  digits = 6\n  label = \"Counter\"\n  max = 10000\n  value = 1234.5","title":"Numeric controls and indicators"},{"category":"section","location":"widgets/#Boolean-controls-and-indicators","page":"Widgets","text":"LED(true; label = \"Run\")\nLED (led) id=\"awi-56f08745-d52f-410c-8cd6-8243e0c1b921\"\n  label = \"Run\"\n  value = true\n\nPushButton(; text = \"START\", color = \"green\", label = \"Start\")\nPushButton (pushbutton) id=\"awi-6073fc67-b65a-4c1a-be14-ff31bd499897\"\n  color = \"green\"\n  label = \"Start\"\n  text = \"START\"\n\nStackLight(; tiers = [\"red\", \"amber\", \"green\"], value = [\"off\", \"blink\", \"on\"], label = \"Stack light\")\nStackLight (stacklight) id=\"awi-47bef7a0-1fb8-43fe-ae5a-e29fcab5aa02\"\n  label = \"Stack light\"\n  tiers = Any[\"red\", \"amber\", \"green\"]\n  value = Any[\"off\", \"blink\", \"on\"]","title":"Boolean controls and indicators"},{"category":"section","location":"widgets/#Process-objects","page":"Widgets","text":"Valve(; mode = \"control\", tag = \"XV-101\", label = \"Feed valve\")\nValve (valve) id=\"awi-4d873483-6d3c-48df-a97e-30d6561402ba\"\n  label = \"Feed valve\"\n  mode = \"control\"\n  tag = \"XV-101\"\n\nPIDFaceplate(; tag = \"TIC-101\", unit = \"°C\", pv = 68.0, pv_max = 100, sp = 70.0, op = 42.0, hi = 85,\n             label = \"Jacket temperature\")\nPIDFaceplate (pidfaceplate) id=\"awi-3ddbb99f-77fd-48e6-9f78-009f4802b087\"\n  hi = 85\n  label = \"Jacket temperature\"\n  op = 42.0\n  pv = 68.0\n  pv_max = 100\n  sp = 70.0\n  tag = \"TIC-101\"\n  unit = \"°C\"","title":"Process objects"},{"category":"section","location":"widgets/#Every-class","page":"Widgets","text":"using Markdown\nrows = [\"| Class | Kind | Messages from the host |\", \"|---|---|---|\"]\nfor class in widget_classes()\n    msgs = [m[\"type\"] for m in message_specs(class) if m[\"direction\"] == \"host-to-front\" && m[\"type\"] != \"hb\"]\n    push!(rows, \"| `$class` | `$(traits(instrument(class))[\"_kind\"])` | $(join(msgs, \", \")) |\")\nend\nMarkdown.parse(join(rows, \"\\n\"))\n                 Class            Kind  Messages from the host\n  –––––––––––––––––––– ––––––––––––––– –––––––––––––––––––––––\n           \u001b[36mAlarmBanner\u001b[39m     \u001b[36malarmbanner\u001b[39m                        \n        \u001b[36mAlarmIndicator\u001b[39m  \u001b[36malarmindicator\u001b[39m                        \n             \u001b[36mAlarmList\u001b[39m       \u001b[36malarmlist\u001b[39m                        \n       \u001b[36mAnalogIndicator\u001b[39m \u001b[36manalogindicator\u001b[39m                        \n           \u001b[36mAnnunciator\u001b[39m     \u001b[36mannunciator\u001b[39m                        \n              \u001b[36mBarGraph\u001b[39m        \u001b[36mbargraph\u001b[39m                        \n              \u001b[36mBitField\u001b[39m        \u001b[36mbitfield\u001b[39m                        \n               \u001b[36mCompass\u001b[39m         \u001b[36mcompass\u001b[39m                        \n    \u001b[36mDeviationIndicator\u001b[39m       \u001b[36mdeviation\u001b[39m                        \n                  \u001b[36mDial\u001b[39m            \u001b[36mdial\u001b[39m                        \n  \u001b[36mDigitalWaveformGraph\u001b[39m    \u001b[36mdigitalgraph\u001b[39m                    data\n         \u001b[36mEmergencyStop\u001b[39m   \u001b[36memergencystop\u001b[39m           latch_expired\n         \u001b[36mEquipmentTree\u001b[39m   \u001b[36mequipmenttree\u001b[39m                        \n              \u001b[36mEventLog\u001b[39m        \u001b[36meventlog\u001b[39m                        \n             \u001b[36mFillSlide\u001b[39m       \u001b[36mfillslide\u001b[39m                        \n                 \u001b[36mGauge\u001b[39m           \u001b[36mgauge\u001b[39m                        \n        \u001b[36mIntensityChart\u001b[39m  \u001b[36mintensitychart\u001b[39m append, snapshot, clear\n               \u001b[36mKPITile\u001b[39m         \u001b[36mkpitile\u001b[39m        snapshot, append\n                  \u001b[36mKnob\u001b[39m            \u001b[36mknob\u001b[39m                        \n                   \u001b[36mLED\u001b[39m             \u001b[36mled\u001b[39m           latch_expired\n                 \u001b[36mMeter\u001b[39m           \u001b[36mmeter\u001b[39m                        \n      \u001b[36mMixedSignalGraph\u001b[39m      \u001b[36mmixedgraph\u001b[39m                    data\n                 \u001b[36mMotor\u001b[39m           \u001b[36mmotor\u001b[39m                        \n          \u001b[36mNumericEntry\u001b[39m    \u001b[36mnumericentry\u001b[39m                        \n          \u001b[36mPIDFaceplate\u001b[39m    \u001b[36mpidfaceplate\u001b[39m                rejected\n        \u001b[36mPictureControl\u001b[39m         \u001b[36mpicture\u001b[39m                    draw\n                  \u001b[36mPipe\u001b[39m            \u001b[36mpipe\u001b[39m                        \n             \u001b[36mPolarPlot\u001b[39m           \u001b[36mpolar\u001b[39m                        \n                  \u001b[36mPump\u001b[39m            \u001b[36mpump\u001b[39m                        \n            \u001b[36mPushButton\u001b[39m      \u001b[36mpushbutton\u001b[39m           latch_expired\n            \u001b[36mRadarChart\u001b[39m           \u001b[36mradar\u001b[39m                        \n           \u001b[36mRecipeTable\u001b[39m     \u001b[36mrecipetable\u001b[39m                rejected\n          \u001b[36mRockerSwitch\u001b[39m    \u001b[36mrockerswitch\u001b[39m           latch_expired\n        \u001b[36mSelectorSwitch\u001b[39m  \u001b[36mselectorswitch\u001b[39m                        \n          \u001b[36mSevenSegment\u001b[39m    \u001b[36msevensegment\u001b[39m                        \n           \u001b[36mSlideSwitch\u001b[39m     \u001b[36mslideswitch\u001b[39m           latch_expired\n            \u001b[36mSmithChart\u001b[39m           \u001b[36msmith\u001b[39m                        \n             \u001b[36mSparkline\u001b[39m       \u001b[36msparkline\u001b[39m        snapshot, append\n            \u001b[36mStackLight\u001b[39m      \u001b[36mstacklight\u001b[39m                        \n          \u001b[36mStateMachine\u001b[39m    \u001b[36mstatemachine\u001b[39m                rejected\n              \u001b[36mSvgPanel\u001b[39m        \u001b[36msvgpanel\u001b[39m                        \n        \u001b[36mSynopticCanvas\u001b[39m        \u001b[36msynoptic\u001b[39m                        \n                  \u001b[36mTank\u001b[39m            \u001b[36mtank\u001b[39m                        \n           \u001b[36mThemeSwitch\u001b[39m     \u001b[36mthemeswitch\u001b[39m                        \n           \u001b[36mThermometer\u001b[39m     \u001b[36mthermometer\u001b[39m                        \n          \u001b[36mToggleSwitch\u001b[39m    \u001b[36mtoggleswitch\u001b[39m           latch_expired\n           \u001b[36mTransmitter\u001b[39m     \u001b[36mtransmitter\u001b[39m                        \n            \u001b[36mTrendChart\u001b[39m      \u001b[36mtrendchart\u001b[39m append, snapshot, clear\n               \u001b[36mVUMeter\u001b[39m         \u001b[36mvumeter\u001b[39m                        \n                 \u001b[36mValve\u001b[39m           \u001b[36mvalve\u001b[39m                        \n         \u001b[36mWaveformChart\u001b[39m   \u001b[36mwaveformchart\u001b[39m append, snapshot, clear\n               \u001b[36mXYGraph\u001b[39m         \u001b[36mxygraph\u001b[39m                    data","title":"Every class"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Shared-rules","page":"Shared rules","text":"Some rules are implemented by the Python kernel, the TypeScript front end and this package. The three are checked against the same parity cases (tests/parity/*.json of anywidget-instruments, copied into test/parity/).","title":"Shared rules"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Alarm-levels","page":"Shared rules","text":"alarm_level computes the level of a value from the lolo, lo, hi and hihi limits (ALARM-002). Limits are inclusive; entering a more severe level is immediate, and leaving a level requires the value to move back beyond that level's limit by at least deadband (ALARM-003).\n\nusing AnywidgetInstruments\nlevels = String[]\nprevious = \"normal\"\nfor v in (81, 79, 78.5, 78, 80)\n    global previous = alarm_level(v; hi = 80, deadband = 2, previous = previous)\n    push!(levels, previous)\nend\nlevels\n5-element Vector{String}:\n \"hi\"\n \"hi\"\n \"hi\"\n \"normal\"\n \"hi\"\n\nWhen the host owns the state (non-empty _session), widgets with an alarm_level trait update it themselves:\n\nt = Tank(50.0; hi = 80, deadband = 2, _session = \"s1\")\nt[:value] = 81\nt[:alarm_level]\n\"hi\"","title":"Alarm levels"},{"category":"section","location":"rules/#Values","page":"Shared rules","text":"coerce_value: a value clamped to [min, max] when coerce is set (NUM-006, NUM-010).\nvalid_scale: finite bounds, max > min, and min > 0 on a logarithmic scale.\nnormalize_value_labels, value_label_of, value_of_label: named values of a scale (IND-118).\n\nlabels = normalize_value_labels([Dict(\"value\" => 2, \"label\" => \"HIGH\"), Dict(\"value\" => 0, \"label\" => \"OFF\")])\nvalue_label_of(labels, 2, 0, 2), value_of_label(labels, \" off \")\n(\"HIGH\", 0.0)","title":"Values"},{"category":"section","location":"kaimonslate/#Kaimon-Slate","page":"Kaimon Slate","text":"Kaimon Slate is a reactive Julia notebook. Its SlateAFM extension hosts anywidget front-end modules; with SlateExtensionsBase loaded, AnywidgetInstruments.jl plugs into it through a package extension:\n\n@bind name Tank(...) binds name to the widget's trait dictionary, rendered by SlateAFM's host shim (kind SlateAFM.AFM);\nthe front end is served from the package, under /ext-assets/AnywidgetInstrumentsSlateExt/;\nsend_message goes through SlateAFM.afm_emit.\n\nThe extension needs Julia 1.12 or later (a requirement of SlateExtensionsBase).","title":"Kaimon Slate"},{"category":"section","location":"kaimonslate/#Setup","page":"Kaimon Slate","text":"SlateAFM lives in the KaimonSlate.jl repository. Add it to the notebook environment with AnywidgetInstruments.jl:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.add(url = \"https://github.com/kahliburke/KaimonSlate.jl\", subdir = \"examples/extensions/SlateAFM\")\nPkg.add(url = \"https://github.com/s-celles/AnywidgetInstruments.jl\")\n\nThen, in the notebook:\n\nusing SlateAFM\nusing AnywidgetInstruments","title":"Setup"},{"category":"section","location":"kaimonslate/#Binding-widgets","page":"Kaimon Slate","text":"@bind inflow Knob(0.05; min = 0, max = 0.2, step = 0.01, unit = \"m³/s\", label = \"Inflow\")\n@bind level Tank(0.0; max = 4, unit = \"m\", hi = 3.5, show_limits = true, label = \"LT-101\")\n\ninflow is the trait dictionary of the knob, reactive: a cell reading inflow[\"value\"] reruns when the operator turns the knob.\n\nTo change a widget from Julia, write its dictionary back with Slate's set_bind; merge_traits checks the new traits against the contract:\n\nset_bind(:level, merge_traits(level; value = 2.4))","title":"Binding widgets"},{"category":"section","location":"kaimonslate/#Messages","page":"Kaimon Slate","text":"Data that travel as messages (trend samples, sparkline values, KPI history) need a message id: give the widget an id and keep the widget object to build its messages.\n\nconst TREND = TrendChart(; id = \"trend\", span = 120, pens = [Dict(\"name\" => \"Level\", \"unit\" => \"m\")])\n@bind trend TREND\n\nsend_message(TREND, append_message(TREND, [[time()]], [[level[\"value\"]]]))\n\nMessages sent by the widgets (operator actions, sync_request) arrive through SlateAFM: SlateAFM.afm_on_msg(\"trend\") do content, buffers … end.","title":"Messages"},{"category":"section","location":"kaimonslate/#Authority-over-the-state","page":"Kaimon Slate","text":"When _session is empty (the default), the front end computes the derived traits (alarm_level, …) itself. With a non-empty _session, the host owns the state: AnywidgetInstruments.jl then updates alarm_level whenever the value or the limits change, with the rule of the front end (see Shared rules).","title":"Authority over the state"},{"category":"section","location":"kaimonslate/#Example","page":"Kaimon Slate","text":"examples/kaimonslate/tank_station.jl in the repository is a complete notebook: a tank filled by a pump, simulated in Julia, with a knob, a tank, a pump and a trend chart. examples/kaimonslate/validate.jl runs it headless:\n\njulia --project=examples/kaimonslate examples/kaimonslate/validate.jl","title":"Example"},{"category":"section","location":"","page":"Home","text":"<div id=\"landing\" class=\"landing\">\n<header class=\"landing-hero\">\n  <div class=\"landing-hero__text\">\n    <p class=\"landing-name\" style=\"--landing-name-chars: 23\">AnywidgetInstruments.jl</p>\n    <h1 class=\"landing-title\">Instrumentation widgets for Julia</h1>\n    <p class=\"landing-tagline\">Knobs, gauges, tanks, LEDs, strip charts, alarms and supervisory objects, from the front end of anywidget-instruments. No Python, no Node.js.</p>\n    <div class=\"landing-actions\">\n<a class=\"landing-btn landing-btn--brand\" href=\"getting-started/\">Getting started</a>\n      <a class=\"landing-btn landing-btn--alt\" href=\"widgets/\">Widgets</a>\n      <a class=\"landing-btn landing-btn--alt\" href=\"https://github.com/s-celles/AnywidgetInstruments.jl\">View on GitHub</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<section class=\"landing-features\" aria-label=\"Features\">\n  <a class=\"landing-feature\" href=\"widgets/\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">🎛️</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">52 widgets</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Every concrete widget of anywidget-instruments has a constructor, Tank(3.2; max = 4), documented from the trait contract.</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"landing-feature\" href=\"getting-started/\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">✅</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Checked traits</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Unknown traits and invalid values fail early with an ArgumentError; numbers are clamped like the front end does.</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"landing-feature\" href=\"getting-started/#Displaying-widgets\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">🌐</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Standalone HTML</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Widgets display in Documenter, VS Code, Jupyter or any HTML page, self-contained.</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"landing-feature\" href=\"kaimonslate/\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">📓</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Kaimon Slate</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Bind widgets with @bind through SlateAFM; drive them from Julia with messages and binary buffers.</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"landing-feature\" href=\"rules/\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">🚨</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Shared rules</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">Alarm levels with deadband, value coercion and value labels, checked against the parity cases of the Python and TypeScript sides.</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"landing-feature\" href=\"specification/\">\n<div class=\"landing-feature__icon\">📐</div>\n<h2 class=\"landing-feature__title\">Specified</h2>\n<p class=\"landing-feature__details\">EARS requirements with MoSCoW priorities, each covered by a test item.</p>\n  </a>\n</section>\n</div>\n\n(Image: Some widgets of AnywidgetInstruments.jl)\n\nAnywidgetInstruments.jl is the Julia host of anywidget-instruments, instrumentation widgets for computational notebooks built on anywidget. The package ships the widgets' front-end module and their trait contract: a widget is a class and a dictionary of traits checked against that contract.\n\nusing AnywidgetInstruments\n\ngain = Knob(2.5; min = 0, max = 10, step = 0.1, unit = \"dB\", label = \"Gain\")\nlevel = Tank(1.2; max = 5, unit = \"m\", lo = 0.5, hi = 4.5, show_limits = true, label = \"Level\")\nhtml_page(\"station.html\", gain, level, LED(true; label = \"Run\"))\n\nwarning: Visualization only\nThese widgets are for monitoring, teaching and prototyping. They are not a protection layer and never replace the safety functions of a process. See the safety notice of anywidget-instruments.","title":"Home"}]
}
